}}|subdivision_type1=[[Communities of Balisca|Community]]|subdivision_name1={{flag|Cerdanya}}|area_km2=26781|population_census=4,792,897|population_census_year=2025|regional_languages=|common_languages=[[Mozarabic]], [[Baliscano]], {{W|Catalan language|Catalan}}, {{W|Occitan language|Occitan}}|cctld=.mta|government_type={{W|Liquid democracy}}|mapsize=280px|ethnic_groups_year=2023|ethnic_groups=58.6% [[Baliscans]]<br/> 41.4% [[Demographics of Balisca|others]]|population_census_rank=12th}}'''Muntanya''' (Catalan pronunciation: {{W|IPA|/monˈtaɲa/, [mõn̪ˈt̪a.ɲa]''}}) is a [[Regions of Balisca|region]] in central [[Cerdanya]], within the [[Baliscan Confederation]]. It borders the [[Máfil]] region to the south, the [[Provence]] region to the west and the [[Dríadas]] and [[Cadaqués]] regions to the north. It has an area of {{convert|26781|km2|mi2|abbr=on}} making it the # largest region of Balisca, and a population of 4,792,897 in the [[2025 Baliscan census|2025 census]]. The administrative seat and largest city is [[Poble]].

The area that became Muntanya was first inhabited by groups of hunter–gatherers 13,000 years ago. The predominant indigenous population prior to the arrival of Europeans were the {{W|Mapuche|Mapuche people}}. Muntanya was colonized relatively late in comparison to other regions of Balisca, beginning with the establishment of Poble in 1714.  

